  "notes": "{啜|すす}る means to slurp or sip by drawing liquid or noodles into the mouth with a sucking action. It also extends to sniffling.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: [food/drink]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{麺|めん}→麺：14644_men⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る: to slurp noodles\n- ⟦スープ→スープ：00395_suupu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る: to sip soup\n- ⟦お{茶|ちゃ}→お茶：00576_ocha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る: to sip tea\n- ⟦{鼻|はな}→鼻：02164_hana⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る: to sniffle, to sniff\n- ⟦{蕎麦|そば}→蕎麦：14329_soba⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{啜|すす}る: to slurp soba noodles\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nSlurping noodles is considered acceptable and even desirable in Japanese dining culture. It is thought to enhance the flavor and show appreciation for the food. This contrasts with Western table manners where slurping is often considered rude.\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {啜|すす} is uncommon; often written in hiragana as すする.",
